{
  "schemaVersion": 3,
  "id": "flutter",
  "name": "Flutter",
  "tagline": "Deep Work with a fast shimmer on the pad and chords.",
  "description": "Deep Work with its dark pad and dub chords fluttering at eight pulses a beat: a fast, soft shimmer locked to the tempo. The flutter fades in once the beat is established, and comes and goes with the tides.",
  "use": {
    "name": "Hold",
    "for": "Days when attention keeps slipping away.",
    "why": "Most brainwave-frequency claims fail. An EEG band is a sign of a state, not a dial for it; binaural beats mostly do not entrain the brain, and failed a direct test of sustained attention; 40 Hz audio has no established focus benefit. What the brain does follow is a sound's envelope, how fast its loudness moves. The one controlled test of that in focus music found a 16 Hz flutter locked to the beat helped sustained attention, but only in listeners with more ADHD symptoms (company-run, a fragile result, not replicated; 32 Hz and faster did worse). So here the pad and chords flutter at eight pulses a beat, 16 Hz at this tempo, arriving gradually and receding in the tides. For other listeners it may do nothing, or mildly distract: that is the experiment."
  },
